WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:06.130
The turmoil in Caracas has subsided for now.
But burned-out vehicles serve as a reminder

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:11.030
of what happened here the day before.
Thousands took to the streets to demonstrate

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.460
against the government. More than two dozen
protesters were killed. Opposition leader

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:23.009
Juan Guaido declared himself caretaker president
and vowed to end what he called "a dictatorship",

00:00:23.009 --> 00:00:30.000
before disappearing to an unknown location.
While many western countries agree with Guaido,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.910
Maduro's own international allies have thrown
their weight behind his socialist government,

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:40.160
with Maduro acknowledging the backing of Russian
president Vladimir Putin.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:47.700
"Russia gives its full support to the legitimate
and constitutional government that I preside

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:56.800
over, its full support for peace and the integrity
and sovereignty of Venezuela. Putin told me:

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:05.780
'President Maduro, you can count on the unwavering
support of Russia.' And now, more than ever,

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.250
we will be working on bilateral projects to
further develop Venezuela."

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:17.479
On the other side, the United States seeks
to increase pressure on Maduro by starving

00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:24.789
his regime of funds.
What we're focusing on today is disconnecting

00:01:24.789 --> 00:01:31.750
the illegitimate Maduro regime from the sources
of its revenues. We think consistent with

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:38.920
our recognition of Juan Guaido as the constitutional
interim president of Venezuela, that those

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.740
revenues should go to the legitimate government.
Washington ordered some of its diplomatic

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.720
staff to leave Caracas, but refused to comply
with a full expulsion as ordered by Maduro.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:55.999
Meanwhile, Maduro has been reaffirmed by both
the Supreme Court and the military. But Guaido

00:01:55.999 --> 00:02:01.549
didn't shy from commenting on Maduro's future
in a televised interview from an undisclosed

00:02:01.549 --> 00:02:11.240
location.
Are you also offering amnesty to Nicolas Maduro?

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:15.090
That would have to be looked at.&nbsp;&nbsp;He is
also a public employee. Unfortunately, he

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:20.890
is a dictator and responsible for yesterday's
victims.

00:02:20.890 --> 00:05:37.729
Venezuelans on both sides now await Guaido's

00:05:37.729 --> 00:08:15.589
next move.

